<title>UK: UK adds to tobacco duty, holds alcohol.</title>
<headline>UK adds to tobacco duty, holds alcohol.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that it would raise tobacco duties from December 1 by a further two percentage points above the annual three percent real rate of increase established by the previous government.</p>
<p>Brown told Parliament this would mean that the price of a packet of 20 cigarettes would rise by 19 pence on November 1 compared with 14 pence under existing proposals.</p>
<p>He said alcohol duties would rise by inflation only from January, while a review of all alcohol and tobacco duties is undertaken, taking account of cross-border shopping.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
